-**Parameters:**
-*   `resolution`: Size of the 1D lookup table. Default value in some loaders is 1024 [S7, unofficial]. Typical values are powers of two (256, 1024, 8192) [S6, S8, unofficial].
-*   `s_min`, `s_range`: The minimum and range of the scalar data domain, used for normalization [S4, unofficial].
-
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Out-of-bounds:** Values outside the normalized $[0, 1]$ range must be clamped to the nearest boundary entry to prevent memory errors [S3, S7, unofficial].
-*   **Color Artifacts:** Interpolating colors directly in RGB space (as in 3D Color Cube Interpolation) can produce unintended colors (e.g., purple between red and blue) that are not in the defined colorbar [S2, unofficial]. 1D TF avoids this by interpolating indices or using 1D texture mapping [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Alpha Combination:** Using `max` for combining Gaussian and control alpha overrides lower opacity but does not attenuate it [S7, unofficial].
-*   **Binning Misalignment:** Using different binning strategies (center vs. edge) for color and alpha can cause slight misalignment at boundaries [S7, unofficial].
